                           <q xml:lang="gez">ዝመጽሐፍ፡ ዘወሐቦ፡ ለኢየሱስ፡ ዘሥላሴ፡ ወብእሲቱ፡ ወለተ፡ ሩፋኤል፡</q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a3">
                           <locus from="72ra" to="72b"/>
                           <desc>An ownership note extended by a record concerning the construction of a church. It mentions that the donation of the manuscript and the construction
                              of the church of the Saviour of the World (possibly in the vicinity of
                              <placeName ref="INS0117GBI">ʾIyasus Gʷaḥgot</placeName> , see  <bibl><ptr target=" bm:Nosnitsin2013Churches"/></bibl>), or in ʾAqāqi near Addis Ababa, 
                              see <bibl><ptr target="bm:Coppet1930ChrMenelik"/><citedRange unit="page">524</citedRange></bibl>GueCopMen, vol. 2, p.
                              524) took place in <date calendar="ethiopian" when-custom="1894" notBefore="1901" notAfter="1902">1894 A.M. (= 1901/1902 A.D.)</date>, in the year of
                              Mark the Evangelist, during the reign of King <persName ref="PRS7006Menilek">Mǝnilǝk II</persName> (r. 1889–1913),
                              when the teacher was mamhǝr Walda ʿAbiya ʾƎgziʿ and his assistant was
                              ʾalaqā ʾAśrat. The note is written in a poor hand, the same as that of <ref target="#a2"/>.
                           </desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ዝንቱ፡ ድርሳን፡ ዘመድኃኔ፡ ዓለም፡ ወኅንፀተ፡
                              ቤተ፡ ክ{ር}ስቲያኑኒ፡ ኮነ፡ በ፲፻ወ፰፻፺ወ፬ቱ፡ አመ{ተ}፡ ምሕረት፡ ዘመኑሂ፡ ማርቆስ፡ ወንጉሡኒ፡ ንጉሠ፡
                              ነገሥት፡ ምኒልክ፡ መምሕሩኒ፡ መምህር፡ ወልደ፡ ዐቢየ፡ እግዚእ፡ አፈ፡ መምሕሩኒ፡ አለቃ፡ አሥራት</q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a4">
                           <locus target="#72v"/>
                           <desc type="RecordTransaction">Record concerning the acquisition of land and the introduction of a new tābot.
                              It states that there are four plots of land with sorghum donated by four individuals
                              (mentioned by name) for (the commemoration of ?) the Saviour of the World. One of the plots should be allocated as a salary for a deacon.
                              Subsequently, it contains a directive which requires that if a new tābot is introduced, it should be dedicated to St George. 
                              The note is written in Amharic, in a mediocre hand. 
                           </desc>
                           <q xml:lang="am">ለመድኃኔ፡ ዓለም፡ የተተካ፡ መሬት፡ ፬፡ ነው፡ ግራ[ት]፡ ምሸላ፡ ከአቶ፡ ይረስ፡ ያለች፡ ከአቶ፡ ተክለ፡ ሃይማኖት፡ ደሞ፡ ያለች፡ ደሞ፡ ከአቶ፡ ሐጐስ፡ ያለች፡ ፬፡
                              ማለታችን፡ ይኅ፡ ነው፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
