               <provenance>The name of the original donor(s) was
                  probably written in the erased part of <ref target="#a1"/> and in the supplication
                  formulas throughout the manuscript. According to <ref target="#a2"/>, Za-Śǝllāse donated
                  the manuscript to the church of <placeName ref="INS0117GBI">ʾIyasus (Gʷaḥgot)</placeName> in 
                  <date calendar="ethiopian" when-custom="1894" notBefore="1901" notAfter="1902">1894 A.M. (= 1901/1902 A.D.)</date>. 
                  His name and the name of his wife Walatta Rufāʾel are also written in the supplication formulas, over
                  the erased name(s), in the same hand as <ref target="#a2"/> (e.g., <locus target="#7ra #32ra"/>). Two other names, Mikāʾel and his wife
                     Ṣadāla Māryām, are added in some supplication formulas, in another secondary
                     hand (e.g., <locus target="#25ra #37va"/>).</provenance></history>
